# PART 5 — STUDENT LIST CONVERTER: FULLY FRONTEND-ONLY

This is a strict requirement.

The HOD must be able to upload student documents and convert them into standard Excel entirely within the browser.

**No Java backend, PostgreSQL, cloud OCR endpoint or external AI service must be required for document conversion.**

The converter must continue working before and after Java backend integration.

Connecting the later Java backend must NOT break or redirect the local document conversion process.

## 5.1 Existing location

HOD Portal → Setup Class → Student Lists → Student List PDF / Image-to-Excel Conversion Helper.

Preserve the existing converter interface and improve its real implementation.

## 5.2 Supported input formats

Support:
- Text-based PDF.
- Scanned PDF.
- JPG/JPEG.
- PNG.
- Multi-page PDF.

Use the actual uploaded file content.

Do not use filenames to produce hardcoded records.

## 5.3 Browser-side conversion architecture

Perform the full conversion within the browser using real client-side processing libraries.

Suitable libraries include:

- `pdfjs-dist` for PDF text extraction and rendering.
- `tesseract.js` for client-side OCR.
- Browser Canvas APIs for image processing.
- An actual XLSX generation library for Excel creation.

Package PDF workers, OCR workers, WASM files and OCR language data locally where practical.

Do not depend on remote OCR services or CDN downloads during conversion.

Do not send the original student PDF or image to Java backend endpoints.

Do not use external Gemini/GPT APIs.

Use Web Workers where appropriate to prevent large PDF processing from freezing the UI.

Use actual processing progress rather than simulated progress.

## 5.4 Standard Student Excel Template

Every converted student list must use exactly these columns:

1. USN.
2. Student Name.
3. DOB.

Example:

| USN | Student Name | DOB |
|---|---|---|
| 4MH24CS071 | Aarav Deshmukh | 2006-03-12 |
| 4MH24CS072 | Bhavana Krishnamurthy | 2006-06-19 |

These are illustrative records only.

The following context must come from the interface and authenticated account:

- Department: Authenticated HOD account.
- Semester: Selected Setup Class semester.
- Section: Selected Student Lists section tab.

Do not add Department, Semester or Section as standard Excel columns.

## 5.5 Document Metadata Detection

If an uploaded PDF contains:

- Department.
- Semester.
- Section.

Extract these separately as document metadata.

Compare against:
- Authenticated HOD department.
- Selected semester.
- Selected section.

Do not insert document metadata as student records.

If metadata conflicts, display a blocking mismatch error.

If a PDF contains students belonging to different sections, do not silently mix them into the selected section.

Request correction or separate processing.

## 5.6 Student extraction

Identify the actual student table structure.

Support different:
- Column widths.
- Fonts.
- Table layouts.
- Page layouts.
- Date formats.
- Multiple-page records.

Do not blindly map consecutive text lines into USN, name and DOB.

