## 9.3 Approval Boundary

The HOD may submit a correction request only.

The HOD cannot:
- Approve their own request.
- Reject their own request.
- Directly modify the examination answer key.
- Manually change student marks.
- Recalculate results.
- Release examination results.

Send the request to the separate COE Portal through the existing backend integration contract.

Only COE-authorised users can approve or reject the correction.

The Java backend must enforce this permission independently.

On COE approval:
- Update the examination-specific answer key.
- Recalculate all impacted results.
- Use stable Question IDs.
- Recalculate across A–D versions and relevant sittings.
- Preserve historical answer-key revisions.
- Record correction approval and recalculation in the audit trail.
- Require COE review before result release.

Do not modify the original master question-bank answer key because of an examination-specific correction.

